        "notes": "Checked all six proof steps and all twelve current supplier interfaces independently. In 1.1 h=u k is a bijection, with (u^-1 g)^-1=g^-1 u; in 2.1 x=u.y is bijective by the action inverse laws. Finite support or coordinatewise absolute convergence permits both reindexings, without interchanging infinite channel sums. First-layer output is group-indexed while input is lattice-indexed. Unit stride/full lattice identifies translation correlation, fixed origin commutes with translations and constant bias is fixed. Steps 1.2/1.3 correctly use right neighborhoods and left cosets; restriction guarantees only subgroup equivariance and finite H=G yields a singleton invariant. Compatible-action composition is proved and finite-grid compatibility remains explicit. Zero filters, trivial groups/subgroups, singleton neighborhoods and empty finite stacks cause no counterexample; no AC or normality is needed. Checked square arrows X->Y, T_u down X and Tprime_u down Y: both paths equal the stated intertwining equation, independent of proof. Cohen–Welling §§2,4–6 equations 1,4–5,7–12,14–17 support conventions; reader/refuter findings empty. Only reader change was contract quotation normalization to the corrected point-group supplier; source is unchanged and sound."
