          "id": "fixed-filter-rotation-witness",
          "claim": "Since $\\rho(0)=0$, $L_\\rho\\delta_0=\\delta_0$. In the displayed planar correlation, only $y=0$ contributes, and $\\delta_{e_1}(e_1)=1$, so $\\delta_0\\star\\delta_{e_1}=\\delta_{-e_1}$. Therefore $L_\\rho(\\delta_0\\star\\delta_{e_1})=\\delta_{\\rho(-e_1)}=\\delta_{-e_2}$, whereas $(L_\\rho\\delta_0)\\star\\delta_{e_1}=\\delta_{-e_1}$. As $e_1\\ne e_2$, these outputs differ.",
