        "notes": "Checked Example and steps 1.1–2.1 against all four current dependencies. U={e,rho} is nonempty finite; pair multiplication proves the four origin rotations form H. Multiplying (t,rho^r)(0,rho^j) leaves t fixed and visits all four rotations, identifying left cosets with translation positions without assuming H normal. The induced full G action on G/H is affine, so orientation pooling remains equivariant, not rotation-invariant at each fixed position. Restriction guarantees H-equivariance only; the separate H=G finite case has one coset and is not applied to infinite p4. Constant/zero features and trivial subgroup cases in suppliers agree; no AC. Cohen–Welling §6.3 eqs.16–17 and its p4/R example support conventions. Reader/refuter findings empty. Native source unchanged; touched contract only replaces the prior point-group terminology quotation. No defect found."
